# Slim the SteadyDigital *upload* recovery kernel (images/kernel-recovery.img).
#
# Two kernels come out of the flash build. The installed one (kernel.img, in
# the .fwu and the NAND bank it is installed on) runs the goggle, so it keeps
# the full driver set - display, decoder, HDMI. This fragment is for the other
# one only: the recovery a stock unit boots from RAM through the Artosyn HID
# loader (the one-time browser-prepare upload). That kernel just runs the
# firmware-update service over USB to write the bank not holding stock, then
# the unit reboots into the installed kernel; it never drives the display,
# camera, audio or any input device, so those subsystems are dead weight in it.
#
# The HID loader uploads this kernel at a hard ~14.6 KiB/s (full-speed, 15-byte
# frames - see the ar9311 USB notes), so its size is the browser-prepare wait.
# Stripping the headless subsystems and XZ-compressing the embedded initramfs
# takes kernel.img from ~5.74 MiB to ~4.32 MiB (-25%, ~6.4 -> ~4.8 min). The
# outer image stays LZ4 (the vendor bootloader only unpacks gz/lzo/lz4); XZ here
# only changes how the kernel stores its own built-in initramfs.
#
# Kept: USB gadget (DWC2/NCM/ACM/FunctionFS/configfs), MTD/spi-nand, UBI/UBIFS,
# crypto, squashfs + overlayfs, ext4/vfat - the firmware-update path.
# NOT in any defconfig: recovery-kernel.sh applies it to a copy of the flash
# build's kernel tree (./build.sh skyzone-steadydigital-flash recovery), so the
# installed kernel and the .fwu are never slimmed.
#
# Boot-verified 2026-11-22: slim+XZ kernel uploaded over the HID loader,
# bootm'd, and recovery came up (CDC-NCM link + update serial).
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_SND is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT is not set
# CONFIG_HID is not set
# CONFIG_USB_HID is not set
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set
# CONFIG_IKCONFIG is not set
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
# CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER is not set
# (no DEBUG_KERNEL: CONFIG_EXPERT selects it)
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
CONFIG_RD_XZ=y
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_XZ=y
# CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_GZIP is not set
